==English==
{{number box|en|90}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|nynty}}, {{m|enm|nynety}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hundniġontiġ}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*newuntēhundą|t=ninety}}, equivalent to {{af|en|nine|-ty}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|nynty}}, {{m|sco|nynety|t=ninety}}, {{cog|stq|njuugentich|t=ninety}}, {{cog|fy|njoggentich|t=ninety}}, {{cog|nl|negentig|t=ninety}}, {{cog|nds-de|negentig|t=ninety}}, {{cog|de|neunzig|t=ninety}}, {{cog|sv|nittio|t=ninety}}, {{cog|nb|nitti|t=ninety}}, {{cog|nn|nitti|t=ninety}}, {{cog|is|níutíu|t=ninety}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈnaɪn.ti/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈnaɪn.di/|/ˈnaɪn.ti/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ninety.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪnti|aɪndi|s=2}}

===Numeral===
{{head|en|numeral}}

# The cardinal number occurring after [[eighty-nine]] and before [[ninety-one]], represented in Roman numerals as [[XC]] and in Arabic numerals as [[90]].

